    "The 20 input samples measure input-event handling through two animation frames. Median changed from 34.75 to 36.05 ms and P95 from 40.9 to 42.7 ms; this does not demonstrate faster typing.",
    "Backend RSS during the first 400 reads increased: median 61.258 to 77.156 MiB and peak 71.359 to 79.672 MiB. Do not claim lower whole-app or whole-device memory.",
    "Completed-page JavaScript heap changed from 31094524 to 21119688 bytes at one unforced-GC observation per build. This is a point measurement, not a retained-memory guarantee.",
    "The final 30-draft browser retest had a high immediate sample: 58089028 JavaScript bytes and 144730744 embedder bytes. A later natural-GC observation was 28219492 and 3321432 bytes. The exact interval was not recorded; this is not a controlled before/after reclamation rate.",
    "The controlled Node experiment forces GC and confirms that 200 saved draft controllers can become unreachable. It does not predict browser GC timing or OS RSS release.",
    "The backend replay deliberately spaces batches and pauses for inspection and approval. Total wall time is not a model-speed or task-throughput benchmark.",
    "Microbenchmark source digests identify the measured implementation. Later correctness fixes are represented separately by the current source digests and integration tests.",
    "Only synthetic fixture measurements are included. Personal paths, process IDs, session/run IDs, credentials, raw user content, and private API validation are excluded."
